  "$comment": "Tests every affected-only pull-request run executes whatever changed: security, permissions, sandbox, contract, IPC channel and naming. An entry ending in '/' selects every collected Vitest file under that prefix; any other entry is one collected Vitest file. scripts/run-ci-suite.mjs refuses an entry that selects nothing. Full runs (every non-PR event, category merges from integration/* into main, and untrusted selections for PRs into non-integration bases) run the whole suite anyway. PRs into integration/* always keep the best traced selection and this nonempty must-run set, even when discovery fails. The \"out-of-process\" group lists every test that runs repo code in a child process through tsx or bundles it with esbuild, itself or through a test helper it imports: the import graph cannot see what that child or bundle loads, so these run on every pull request (test/scripts/run-ci-suite.test.ts fails when one is missing). The \"tree-invariants\" group lists every test that reads the tracked tree with `git ls-files` and asserts an invariant over it (the must-run set itself, pre-push tiers, repository identity, documentation readers): a test-only change can break one of those invariants without touching the suite, so they run on every pull request and main push (test/scripts/run-ci-suite.test.ts fails when one is missing).",
